WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:01.170
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:02.580
- [Narrator] Former President Donald Trump

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.440
has been in court a lot lately.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.490
- [Reporter 1] Hush money payments.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:06.690
- [Reporter 2] Illegally possessed

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.640
classified government materials.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.640
- His attempt to overturn
the results of an election.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.820
- We have seen nothing
approaching this before,

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.810
with respect to these
indictments of Donald Trump.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.940
- [Narrator] Trump, now faces four trials

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.590
from two federal indictments

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.750
and two state indictments.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.100
Here's how Trump's legal team

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.360
could mount their defense,

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.660
and how these charges could
influence his 2024 bid

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.403
and those of his rivals.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.210
- A Fulton County Grand Jury

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.630
returned a true bill of indictment.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.680
- [Narrator] The Georgia Indictment

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.350
charges the former
president with 13 felonies

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:47.160
for trying to undo his 2020
election defeat in the state.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.830
The probe hinges on a
key piece of evidence,

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:50.970
a recorded phone call,

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.470
then, President Trump made

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.980
to Georgia's Top Elections
Official, Brad Raffensperger,

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.957
- [Trump] I just wanna find 11,780 votes,

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.910
which is one more that we have.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.950
- [Narrator] Trump has said
that, "He did nothing wrong,

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.800
and the call was quote
'Absolutely perfect.'"

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.570
- I think that the strategy here

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:13.980
sort of the umbrella strategy

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:18.270
that it's a quote-unquote,
"Witch hunt on multiple fronts

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:21.360
to stop him from
regaining the presidency."

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.430
That's not really a legal defense

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.380
that's more of a public relations defense,

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.820
but, you know, he obviously has people

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.070
who are buying into that theory.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.570
- [Narrator] One reason
the Georgia Indictment

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.460
is different from the federal cases

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.430
is that even if Trump were
reelected as president.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.470
- Let's presume he's convicted in Georgia,

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:41.220
the Federal Government
President has no pardon power

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.980
over those state convictions.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:44.813
- [Narrator] In Georgia,

00:01:44.813 --> 00:01:46.680
the State Board of Pardons and Paroles,

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.950
doesn't consider pardon
applications until five years

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.830
after an individual has
completed their sentence.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.870
- So he could be conceivably,

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.180
under the most outlandish scenario,

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.100
sitting in prison

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:03.900
and still being the President
of the United States.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.700
- [Narrator] Trump's
alleged conduct in Georgia,

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.040
also plays a role in a federal case,

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.410
accusing him of trying to subvert the will

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.883
of American voters.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:13.860
On August 1st,

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:17.460
Trump was indicted by a Federal
Grand Jury in Washington.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:20.460
The indictment brought by
Special Counsel Jack Smith,

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.370
charges the former president
with four criminal counts

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.960
for his actions that culminated

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.337
in the January 6th Capitol Riot.

00:02:27.337 --> 00:02:28.709
[Crowd] We want Trump.

00:02:28.709 --> 00:02:31.590
We want Trump, we want Trump!

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:32.880
- [Leslie] The January 6th case

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.040
is clearly the most significant case.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.810
It's the most comprehensive.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.730
- The attack on our nation's Capitol,

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.990
on January 6th, 2021

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.980
was an unprecedented assault

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.080
on the seat of American democracy.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.840
- Trump has a right to
challenge the election results.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.060
Trump has a right to speak out,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.030
even lie about the election results.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:56.850
Trump took his right and went to court,

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.040
and lost every single significant case!

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.190
That should have been the end of it.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.510
- We fight like hell,

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.220
and if you don't fight like hell,

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.020
you're not gonna have a country anymore.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.040
- For the defense,

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:11.490
they've already laid some
seeds for their approach.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.710
One is to delay the case
as long as possible.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.110
The second thing is to
allege that he was merely

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.360
exercising his First Amendment Rights.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.550
And I think, you know, as in
most criminal defense cases,

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.810
and I've been a criminal defense lawyer

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.070
for a number of years myself,

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.440
you try to distract the
jury from the evidence

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.350
by raising things like the First
Amendment and other issues,

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.580
which I think they'll do

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.870
- [Narrator] In a social media post.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.850
Trump said, "The case
was a pathetic attempt

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.110
by the Justice Department

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:37.470
to interfere with the 2024
Presidential Election.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.450
- When you look at what's happening,

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:42.990
this is a persecution
of a political opponent.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.440
This was never supposed
to happen in America.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:47.970
- [Narrator] In June, Trump was indicted

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.400
for his handling of classified documents,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.110
marking the first time in history

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:53.250
that the federal government

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.100
has brought charges
against a former president.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.777
The case, also led by
Jack Smith, alleges that,

00:03:58.777 --> 00:04:01.290
"Trump deliberately
withheld sensitive documents

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.450
at his Mar-a-Lago Resort in Florida,

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:07.440
even after prosecutors requested
their return last year."

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.330
- This is really an
obstruction of justice case,

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.760
this is not a possession of
classified documents case.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.710
Yes, you could have left office

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.480
and accidentally, or on purpose,

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.550
taken some documents
that you shouldn't have,

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.470
but once you know you're
supposed to give them back,

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:22.110
you can't then lie about it and hide them,

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.820
and engage in various schemes,

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.790
enlisting other people
to help you do that.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:27.697
- [Narrator] Trump has complained that,

00:04:27.697 --> 00:04:29.460
"He is being treated unfairly.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.530
Since classified documents have been found

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:34.470
in the possession of other
high-ranking politicians."

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:37.380
- They've tried to create
a false equivalency

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.800
between Trump's handling of documents

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.080
and the handling of documents by others.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.420
Okay, while Mike Pence and Joe Biden

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:46.650
had classified documents,

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.750
which they immediately returned

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.280
as soon as they were alerted.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.980
- [Narrator] Smith added
new charges on July 27th,

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.140
alleging that, "Trump
and a maintenance worker

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.110
sought to delete surveillance
footage from Mar-a-Lago

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:01.320
so it couldn't be turned
over to a grand jury."

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.470
Trump has said, "He's an innocent man."

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.390
The April indictment of Donald Trump

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:08.790
for allegedly falsifying business records

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.890
marked the first time in US history

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:14.190
that a former president
has faced criminal charges.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.660
- The Manhattan DA's case

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.400
is a case that doesn't necessarily

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.330
have anything to do with the fact

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.040
that Trump was President
of the United States,

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.630
it has to do with the fact that he,

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.960
apparently paid hush money
to a pornography actress,

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.220
and tried to conceal it,

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.720
which, you know, at the end of the day,

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:28.830
he's not the first person,

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.590
nor will he be the last who
does something like that.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:33.000
- [Narrator] Trump has pleaded not guilty

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.510
in the New York, Florida,
and Washington D.C. Cases.

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:40.170
It remains to be seen how each
trial will play out in court.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.690
- Trump's team, I think
that their strategy

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.140
has gotta be to delay as long as possible.

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.640
The other strategy that they have

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:50.850
is to try to try this case in
the court of public opinion,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.350
as opposed to in the courtroom,

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:53.820
where they can make these arguments

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.080
that aren't really legal defenses,

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.530
like "Trump believed
that he actually won,"

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:00.360
and I think that's gonna be hard for them

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.690
to convince a jury unanimously,

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.190
that that was the case here.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:06.090
- [Narrator] Even if the defense

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.040
doesn't convince the entire jury,

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.280
a hung jury could still be
considered a win for Trump.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.500
- All that Trump has to
achieve in any of these cases,

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:17.160
is one juror who's voting
against the other jurors.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.820
So 11 to 1 for him would be a victory,

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:22.357
and then the prosecutor
would have to decide

00:06:22.357 --> 00:06:24.087
"Do I wanna retry this case?"

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.490
- [Narrator] While recent polls show Trump

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.760
has a commanding lead over the
rest of the Republican field,

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.860
his legal troubles have taken a chunk

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.050
out of his campaign finances.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:35.100
Recent data show

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.710
that his main political
committee Save America,

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.780
shelled out more than $20 million

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:42.990
on legal-related expenses
so far this year.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:46.290
But the indictments have
also helped Trump fundraise,

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:48.240
in the days following the indictments,

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:51.870
his campaign contributions
increased by millions.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:54.360
- The critical thing will be the trials,

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.670
and whether he is convicted,

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:58.320
and the conventional wisdom is,

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:00.330
you know, this may help him,

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.910
his base will unite behind him.

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:03.847
They've softened a bit,

00:07:03.847 --> 00:07:05.280
"Yes, we still love Trump,

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:10.280
but do we really want to go
through all of this again

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.020
or do we want to look forward?"

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:14.760
- [Narrator] Trump may
also have to navigate

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:17.580
attending various court
dates while he's campaigning.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:20.070
- It's possible, he could have four trials

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:23.730
before the November Election,

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:26.640
each of which, could take many weeks.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:29.550
In other words, during
the prime campaign season,

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:33.090
he could be tied down in court.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:34.740
- [Narrator] And as for
his political opponents

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.080
on the 2024 Campaign Trail?

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.510
- You know, if DeSantis, and Nikki Haley,

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:41.160
and Tim Scott, and others,

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.340
hope to bring down Trump,
they have to go after him.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.810
Kind of what they've done so far,

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:49.470
tiptoeing around these
incredibly serious charges

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:50.940
against Donald Trump

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:55.275
is gonna do absolutely nothing for them.

00:07:55.275 --> 00:08:00.275
(crowd cheering)
(playful music)

